WEBVTT

00:00:00.870 --> 00:00:01.960
You're...

00:00:02.460 --> 00:00:04.330
Tohru Kazasumi.

00:00:17.850 --> 00:00:20.680
Who the hell is he?

00:00:20.680 --> 00:00:23.020
I suppose you would dodge it, yeah...

00:01:53.170 --> 00:01:57.760
Resolve: An Ending World

00:01:56.740 --> 00:01:59.530
<i>He has the same face as me...
the same voice!</i>

00:02:01.280 --> 00:02:03.750
<i>What is this?
What's going on here?</i>

00:02:11.710 --> 00:02:12.750
Where are you aim—

00:02:17.550 --> 00:02:20.220
This attack... Remy?

00:02:21.390 --> 00:02:24.390
It's not nice to bully the weak.

00:02:24.390 --> 00:02:26.100
H-Hold on...

00:02:26.480 --> 00:02:29.600
C-Can we land on the ground sometime soon?

00:02:30.110 --> 00:02:32.190
<i>Remy, what's your status?</i>

00:02:32.190 --> 00:02:33.980
I saved her.

00:02:34.150 --> 00:02:38.990
She was about to fall, but now 
she's happily floating around.

00:02:40.910 --> 00:02:42.910
This is Kazasumi.
We're retreating.

00:02:45.580 --> 00:02:48.250
<i>Enemy retreat confirmed.</i>

00:02:48.420 --> 00:02:49.330
Roger.

00:02:51.630 --> 00:02:52.540
Are you hurt?

00:02:52.540 --> 00:02:55.130
No, I'm fine.

00:02:55.130 --> 00:02:58.010
Your big brother can be pretty annoying.

00:03:00.090 --> 00:03:03.350
You're one of the first-years, right?

00:03:03.350 --> 00:03:04.600
Your name was...

00:03:04.600 --> 00:03:05.350
Remy.

00:03:05.350 --> 00:03:08.060
Right! You're Remy Odhner!

00:03:08.060 --> 00:03:10.650
You just saved me, right? Thanks!

00:03:11.520 --> 00:03:15.150
What you did just now was amazing!
Were those like, psychic powers?

00:03:15.650 --> 00:03:17.610
You're not afraid of me?

00:03:18.320 --> 00:03:20.530
Afraid? Why?

00:03:21.450 --> 00:03:23.580
Oh right! I have to look for Tohru.

00:03:23.780 --> 00:03:24.830
Excuse me a bit.

00:03:25.200 --> 00:03:26.160
Tohru!

00:03:26.330 --> 00:03:27.160
Tohru!

00:03:27.950 --> 00:03:30.290
Tohru! Are you all right?

00:03:30.920 --> 00:03:34.340
Yeah, it's just a scratch.
What about you?

00:03:38.800 --> 00:03:39.920
Where are we?

00:03:40.260 --> 00:03:43.260
It doesn't seem like a management district...

00:03:43.550 --> 00:03:47.180
Yeah. I've seen this before
in a video we watched in class.

00:03:47.520 --> 00:03:49.390
It's an old, old management district.

00:03:50.390 --> 00:03:52.230
I think they called it Japan...

00:04:00.070 --> 00:04:01.910
W-what's going on here?

00:04:02.110 --> 00:04:04.570
You really don't know anything, do you?

00:04:05.990 --> 00:04:10.370
Just like you said, this is Japan.

00:04:14.880 --> 00:04:18.710
Operator, I'm in the Box with the two of them.
Heading up now.

00:04:18.710 --> 00:04:20.720
<i>Roger that. Commencing transfer.</i>

00:04:24.430 --> 00:04:25.350
<i>Help me.</i>

00:04:25.350 --> 00:04:26.300
It's you!

00:04:26.300 --> 00:04:27.390
<i>The future...</i>

00:04:30.850 --> 00:04:32.350
Wh-What?

00:04:33.690 --> 00:04:34.690
<i>The future...</i>

00:04:42.450 --> 00:04:44.240
I heard it was a traffic accident.

00:04:44.240 --> 00:04:46.160
Both of them together...

00:04:46.660 --> 00:04:49.200
Leaving such a young child behind...

00:04:49.580 --> 00:04:53.370
Your parents' death has been 
ruled a work-related accident.

00:04:53.370 --> 00:04:58.170
In accordance with regulations, your 
expenses will be provided for until you turn 18.

00:04:58.710 --> 00:05:02.300
Tohru, it's okay to cry.

00:05:10.430 --> 00:05:11.930
Consciousness confirmed.

00:05:11.930 --> 00:05:13.810
Awareness levels, normal.

00:05:13.980 --> 00:05:16.730
Good morning, Tohru Kazasumi.

00:05:17.810 --> 00:05:20.480
G-Good morning.

00:05:27.870 --> 00:05:29.740
It's Xi, right?

00:05:30.370 --> 00:05:32.120
The girl I was with,
Kyoka Katagiri—

00:05:32.120 --> 00:05:34.000
Healthy both in mind and spirit.

00:05:34.000 --> 00:05:36.620
I'm telling you, I'll help!

00:05:36.620 --> 00:05:40.210
But Matsurika, you have the
maintenance on Freya to do.

00:05:40.210 --> 00:05:43.840
I leave routine maintenance to the staff.

00:05:43.840 --> 00:05:46.680
I understand that,
but you see...

00:05:46.680 --> 00:05:48.890
I see what?

00:05:49.430 --> 00:05:51.010
Who are those two?

00:05:51.010 --> 00:05:54.100
They are combat personnel
participating in the operation.

00:05:54.560 --> 00:05:55.770
Combat?

00:05:59.190 --> 00:06:00.320
This way.

00:06:03.230 --> 00:06:04.900
Please, come in.

00:06:05.490 --> 00:06:07.950
Welcome, Tohru Kazasumi.

00:06:08.950 --> 00:06:13.330
I'm Brian Odhner,
and I'm the supervisor here.

00:06:13.540 --> 00:06:16.160
You woke up pretty late, didn't you?

00:06:16.160 --> 00:06:19.130
He and Kyoka are irregulars, after all.

00:06:19.960 --> 00:06:24.590
Now, publically, this is a research lab
for the Melchizedek Corporation,

00:06:24.590 --> 00:06:26.800
but that's just a facade...

00:06:30.720 --> 00:06:33.520
We are fighting...

00:06:34.770 --> 00:06:36.230
...to save this world...

00:06:37.640 --> 00:06:41.150
...from ourselves in another universe.

00:06:42.610 --> 00:06:44.650
What is this?

00:06:44.940 --> 00:06:47.490
From the samples gathered on-site,

00:06:47.490 --> 00:06:52.410
it's been proven that the parties concerned
are biologically the same individual.

00:06:55.200 --> 00:06:58.500
In other words, it's not just you.

00:06:59.420 --> 00:07:00.580
Big Brother!

00:07:00.580 --> 00:07:01.250
Yo!

00:07:04.090 --> 00:07:05.710
Instructor, you too?

00:07:05.710 --> 00:07:06.670
Hi!

00:07:09.340 --> 00:07:11.050
Now, Kazasumi.

00:07:11.470 --> 00:07:15.680
I'm sure you've heard the term
"Desert Syndrome" before.

00:07:16.310 --> 00:07:18.690
Yes... just rumors, though.

00:07:19.190 --> 00:07:25.360
It's when the human body suddenly 
turns into sand, and crumbles away...

00:07:27.780 --> 00:07:32.620
We call it the the "Sandification 
Process", AKA "Degradation."

00:07:33.030 --> 00:07:34.330
No way...

00:07:34.330 --> 00:07:35.580
It's real?

00:07:35.580 --> 00:07:40.540
This phenomenon where people turn into sand
is happening all over the globe.

00:07:40.830 --> 00:07:42.710
We have yet to find a solution.

00:07:43.460 --> 00:07:46.960
Ever since it started, the intelligence bureau
has been busy with the cover-up.

00:07:47.090 --> 00:07:49.880
How do you hide something like this?

00:07:49.880 --> 00:07:54.010
They know who's going to disappear, 
so they stay one step ahead.

00:07:54.010 --> 00:07:55.260
How do they do that?

00:07:55.850 --> 00:07:57.600
The Timekeepers.

00:07:58.390 --> 00:08:02.810
Roughly two years ago,
they intruded on our communications.

00:08:03.770 --> 00:08:07.650
<i>An announcement... A warning...
And a notification.</i>

00:08:08.070 --> 00:08:10.990
<i>Encroachment by the primordial 
conclusion has been confirmed.</i>

00:08:11.780 --> 00:08:13.740
<i>Time remaining until the 
primordial conclusion:</i>

00:08:15.950 --> 00:08:22.080
<i>3...9...3...1...</i>

00:08:17.580 --> 00:08:22.080
The time in which we live, itself, 
is about to come to an end.

00:08:23.460 --> 00:08:26.290
And the degredations are a sign of that.

00:08:27.300 --> 00:08:31.630
That was more or less the 
information they gave us.

00:08:31.930 --> 00:08:37.430
That information contained the names of
who was going to disappear and when.

00:08:37.640 --> 00:08:40.520
Everyone is going to turn into sand?

00:08:40.520 --> 00:08:46.060
The times the disappearances occur vary,
but the information continues to be precise.

00:08:47.940 --> 00:08:51.490
Kazasumi, Kyoka,
there's something I want to show you.

00:08:51.900 --> 00:08:54.860
This is top-secret classified information.

00:08:57.700 --> 00:09:00.660
In addition to the warnings they offered,

00:09:00.660 --> 00:09:04.620
the Timekeepers also said they would give 
us technology that would save the world,

00:09:05.080 --> 00:09:10.510
but they would only give it to those 
who were victorious in battle.

00:09:11.420 --> 00:09:12.510
The opponents being...

00:09:12.510 --> 00:09:15.430
...ourselves in another universe.

00:09:19.970 --> 00:09:23.770
We don't know why it's Japan of 2015.

00:09:23.770 --> 00:09:28.440
Don't you think it's these Timekeepers 
who are behind all this?

00:09:28.440 --> 00:09:34.530
Even so, we can't stop the Degradation.
We have to play along with their game.

00:09:34.950 --> 00:09:37.120
But how do we get to Japan?

00:09:37.370 --> 00:09:40.950
That's what our lab is for.

00:09:41.160 --> 00:09:46.500
A spacetime resonance facility developed
with the Timekeepers' technology...

00:09:47.420 --> 00:09:48.170
In other words,

00:09:51.710 --> 00:09:53.170
a time machine!

00:09:58.260 --> 00:10:02.930
We can send qualified individuals to 2015,
and also bring them back.

00:10:03.270 --> 00:10:04.520
Qualified individuals?

00:10:04.730 --> 00:10:07.940
Those rare individuals capable 
of space-time transfers.

00:10:07.940 --> 00:10:10.690
Your measured values were especially high.

00:10:11.320 --> 00:10:15.860
But I never thought you'd be able to 
spacetime transfer without a time machine...

00:10:16.200 --> 00:10:18.030
How in the world did you do it?

00:10:18.450 --> 00:10:20.160
I don't really know.

00:10:20.490 --> 00:10:21.950
I fell from a high place—

00:10:21.950 --> 00:10:22.740
What?

00:10:23.040 --> 00:10:24.950
You simply fell from a high location?

00:10:25.660 --> 00:10:27.080
It's true that, theoretically,

00:10:27.080 --> 00:10:30.630
if you have enough gravitational potential,
you don't need a box space.

00:10:30.790 --> 00:10:32.020
But under fluid boundary conditions—

00:10:32.020 --> 00:10:33.550
Leave that for later!

00:10:33.880 --> 00:10:36.510
You have one more important thing
to discuss, don't you?

00:10:39.050 --> 00:10:44.640
This is the most important over-technology
that the Timekeepers have granted us:

00:10:45.020 --> 00:10:46.730
the Energy Cube.

00:10:46.890 --> 00:10:48.600
Replaying recorded data.

00:10:50.060 --> 00:10:52.770
We're applying the Energy 
Cube to a standard gun.

00:10:57.030 --> 00:10:58.320
Application complete.

00:11:04.870 --> 00:11:05.870
The gun...

00:11:05.870 --> 00:11:07.580
It changed shape?

00:11:07.870 --> 00:11:10.040
To be precise, it "evolved."

00:11:10.500 --> 00:11:16.010
Something you could call "time energy"
is stored within this cube.

00:11:17.590 --> 00:11:22.550
We were told to use this to win our battles.

00:11:22.550 --> 00:11:28.100
We mainly use it for enhancing the weapons
and defensive fields of the combat personnel.

00:11:28.100 --> 00:11:32.060
However, with each battle,
the enemy weapons are getting stronger, too.

00:11:32.650 --> 00:11:34.980
That means they've been given the same thing.

00:11:35.530 --> 00:11:36.820
This is...

00:11:37.150 --> 00:11:38.530
This is all insane!

00:11:38.950 --> 00:11:41.990
Exactly. It's insane.

00:11:42.410 --> 00:11:48.000
Degradation, over-technology, 
forced combat...

00:11:48.500 --> 00:11:50.790
None of these are dreams.

00:11:53.500 --> 00:11:58.260
We're throwing ourselves into battle
as the result of a very difficult decision.

00:11:58.670 --> 00:12:03.640
Unfortunately, we weren't given the 
ability to make the choice for ourselves.

00:12:13.230 --> 00:12:14.900
There are weapons inside.

00:12:15.940 --> 00:12:18.150
They're locked with biometric authentication.

00:12:18.820 --> 00:12:22.280
If you wish to join the 
war, please open them.

00:12:22.660 --> 00:12:25.870
That will indicate your approval 
of the final contract.

00:12:26.660 --> 00:12:30.080
So here you are, troubled young man...

00:12:32.040 --> 00:12:35.090
Hey, let's talk about your future.

00:12:35.670 --> 00:12:38.340
In a place where we can be all alone.

00:12:38.800 --> 00:12:40.970
O-Okay...

00:12:43.090 --> 00:12:46.390
Ma'am, are you a member of that lab?

00:12:46.390 --> 00:12:49.270
Yes. My instructor position 
is merely a front.

00:12:49.470 --> 00:12:52.100
So, have you made up your mind?

00:12:52.890 --> 00:12:56.940
You're telling me the world is going to end,
but it just doesn't feel real to me...

00:12:57.360 --> 00:12:58.320
I'm sure.

00:12:58.940 --> 00:13:02.070
Humans fight only
when they feel the need to.

00:13:02.820 --> 00:13:05.450
The need to fight...

00:13:06.530 --> 00:13:09.660
It's important to think about your future.

00:13:10.120 --> 00:13:11.710
It makes me happy,

00:13:12.040 --> 00:13:14.960
so I'll give you more food for thought.

00:13:17.460 --> 00:13:18.880
What is this?

00:13:18.880 --> 00:13:21.130
Live footage of someone's degradation!

00:13:29.010 --> 00:13:31.890
Th-This is happening right now, isn't it?

00:13:31.890 --> 00:13:33.390
That's what I said.

00:13:35.310 --> 00:13:37.690
What are you trying to accomplish
by showing me this?

00:13:37.690 --> 00:13:42.940
Nothing at all. I'm just showing you
the truth about the world you live in.

00:13:44.280 --> 00:13:48.030
So, are you going to fight 
to save the world? Or...

00:13:48.030 --> 00:13:48.700
I'm—

00:13:54.910 --> 00:13:56.670
Enough playing around!

00:13:57.000 --> 00:14:00.210
Combat between allies
is a breach of contract.

00:14:00.210 --> 00:14:02.630
Is that something that
a criminal like you should say?

00:14:02.880 --> 00:14:04.760
We'll continue this some other time, okay?

00:14:12.470 --> 00:14:14.230
Did you send her?

00:14:14.560 --> 00:14:16.310
You've got some sick hobbies.

00:14:16.310 --> 00:14:18.940
I simply told him the truth.

00:14:19.360 --> 00:14:22.860
I thought you disliked Tohru Kazasumi?

00:14:23.230 --> 00:14:29.450
In a group of morons from high-ranking 
families, he's better than most.

00:14:29.450 --> 00:14:33.120
Then why have you been removing him
from the recruitment list?

00:14:33.750 --> 00:14:35.660
Well, um... that's because...

00:14:35.660 --> 00:14:38.880
If he joins, Kyoka will tag along.

00:14:41.130 --> 00:14:45.260
It's a lot of trouble having a younger sister
that gets out of hand... you and me both.

00:14:45.260 --> 00:14:46.970
Shut up, you sadist.

00:14:49.430 --> 00:14:51.050
Have you calmed down?

00:14:51.220 --> 00:14:52.310
I guess...

00:14:52.470 --> 00:14:57.850
Showing you a live Degradation? 
That's disgusting!

00:15:02.270 --> 00:15:04.030
W-what are those?

00:15:04.030 --> 00:15:06.030
That's Dogma and Magma.

00:15:06.030 --> 00:15:07.780
Aren't they cute?

00:15:09.740 --> 00:15:12.830
This is mint tea.
Drink it while it's hot.

00:15:17.040 --> 00:15:18.620
Lord Tohru Kazasumi.

00:15:19.620 --> 00:15:24.130
On behalf of Lord Kyohma,
I, Sidune Rindo, give you thanks.

00:15:24.630 --> 00:15:27.510
You have protected Lady Kyoka.

00:15:27.510 --> 00:15:29.300
No, it's nothing...

00:15:29.300 --> 00:15:34.560
And I apologize for my family
troubling you earlier.

00:15:34.560 --> 00:15:35.720
Family?

00:15:35.720 --> 00:15:38.230
That woman that calls herself Olga.

00:15:38.230 --> 00:15:40.400
Her real name is Orika Rindo.

00:15:40.400 --> 00:15:45.690
She's a terrorist on the most wanted list...
and my elder sister.

00:15:46.990 --> 00:15:49.400
You two siblings are really quite... unique.

00:15:51.030 --> 00:15:51.950
Um...

00:15:52.160 --> 00:15:54.280
About Lord Kyohma...

00:15:54.580 --> 00:15:57.040
Please don't hate him.

00:15:57.830 --> 00:16:01.420
He may not look it, but he's 
expecting a lot out of you.

00:16:01.420 --> 00:16:02.170
Out of me?

00:16:02.790 --> 00:16:06.340
Lord Kyohma is the next leader
of the Katagiri Group.

00:16:06.760 --> 00:16:12.300
The one who invited Doctor Odhner
and created that lab was Lord Kyohma, too.

00:16:12.800 --> 00:16:16.060
But whenever there's power, there's 
always conflict to go with it.

00:16:16.430 --> 00:16:18.640
Lord Kyohma didn't want that bitc—

00:16:19.680 --> 00:16:21.230
Excuse me!

00:16:21.230 --> 00:16:26.980
He didn't want Lady Kyoka caught up in that,
and has worked hard to avoid it.

00:16:27.280 --> 00:16:29.150
I see...

00:16:29.150 --> 00:16:34.950
So for Lord Kyohma to pick a fight with you
like a child... I'm so jealous!

00:16:34.950 --> 00:16:38.620
I mean, it goes to show how highly
he thinks of you, Tohru!

00:16:43.830 --> 00:16:45.710
A reason to fight?

00:16:46.130 --> 00:16:49.550
They say I've got the 
power to save the world,

00:16:49.710 --> 00:16:51.260
but I just don't understand.

00:16:53.470 --> 00:16:55.850
What if you think of it like this?

00:16:55.850 --> 00:16:59.560
There's always been wars and 
conflicts, all over the world.

00:16:59.930 --> 00:17:04.650
Long before the Degradations started,
this world was already crazy.

00:17:04.980 --> 00:17:08.360
It's not really your responsibility, Tohru.

00:17:09.030 --> 00:17:12.150
So you should do what you want to do.

00:17:13.990 --> 00:17:16.070
Why do you fight?

00:17:16.700 --> 00:17:18.660
I fight for Lord Kyohma.

00:17:19.080 --> 00:17:23.460
As long as I can help him,
I don't care what happens to me.

00:17:25.710 --> 00:17:28.500
You're strong, Sidune...

00:17:28.670 --> 00:17:31.260
My reason is rather selfish.

00:17:31.630 --> 00:17:35.890
One person can't really carry that 
many burdens by themselves, anyway.

00:17:44.020 --> 00:17:45.980
I knew you'd be here!

00:17:46.440 --> 00:17:47.980
I was looking for you!

00:17:48.690 --> 00:17:49.360
I'm sorry.

00:17:50.110 --> 00:17:51.780
I'm glad I found you.

00:17:51.780 --> 00:17:56.160
Well... you know, I wanted to talk.

00:17:56.570 --> 00:17:57.780
Me, too.

00:18:02.290 --> 00:18:08.130
My parents both died when I was 
young... in a traffic accident.

00:18:09.340 --> 00:18:10.090
Yeah.

00:18:10.670 --> 00:18:12.710
I just didn't know what was going on.

00:18:13.340 --> 00:18:15.180
I couldn't feel sad about it, either.

00:18:16.340 --> 00:18:19.430
But, when I heard
I could go back to the past,

00:18:20.180 --> 00:18:21.560
I wanted to see them.

00:18:22.350 --> 00:18:26.440
I thought "I want to see Dad and Mom."

00:18:28.060 --> 00:18:29.360
I see.

00:18:29.360 --> 00:18:31.110
It's such a waste, isn't it?

00:18:31.520 --> 00:18:35.610
They've got a time machine, but 
they can only use it for fighting.

00:18:36.030 --> 00:18:38.660
Yeah. It really doesn't 
make sense, does it?

00:18:41.910 --> 00:18:42.620
Hey...

00:18:43.950 --> 00:18:46.790
Are you going to open the case?

00:18:48.790 --> 00:18:50.790
"Help me," was what she told me.

00:18:51.840 --> 00:18:55.130
Oh... you didn't tell them about that girl.

00:18:55.420 --> 00:18:57.010
You want to help her?

00:18:58.890 --> 00:18:59.930
Why?

00:19:00.390 --> 00:19:01.550
I don't know.

00:19:02.720 --> 00:19:05.890
Tohru, you get so reckless...

00:19:06.140 --> 00:19:07.890
But what about you?

00:19:10.980 --> 00:19:12.820
What should I do, I wonder?

00:19:13.820 --> 00:19:16.400
Thanks for telling me about your parents.

00:19:16.400 --> 00:19:17.610
I was happy you did.

00:19:17.900 --> 00:19:19.700
I'll see you tomorrow.

00:19:26.870 --> 00:19:28.620
Help Me

00:19:38.550 --> 00:19:40.180
<i>We are fighting...</i>

00:19:40.180 --> 00:19:42.510
<i>...to save this world...</i>

00:19:42.510 --> 00:19:44.850
<i>...from ourselves in another universe.</i>

00:19:44.850 --> 00:19:47.390
So, are you going to 
fight to save the world?

00:19:47.390 --> 00:19:49.980
<i>The reason is rather selfish.</i>

00:19:50.230 --> 00:19:51.600
<i>Tohru Kazasumi.</i>

00:20:12.420 --> 00:20:15.630
<i>Authentication complete.
Will you open the case?</i>

00:20:18.880 --> 00:20:21.890
<i>The contract is now complete.
Releasing the lock.</i>

00:21:35.500 --> 00:21:37.420
<i>Whether or not
this is the correct decision...</i>

00:21:38.210 --> 00:21:39.670
<i>I don't know right now.</i>

00:21:41.340 --> 00:21:42.220
<i>But...</i>

00:21:42.920 --> 00:21:44.680
<i>I'll do everything I can.</i>

00:23:25.490 --> 00:23:27.200
We should end this.

00:23:27.200 --> 00:23:29.530
A sudden breakup! A turning point in life!

00:23:29.530 --> 00:23:31.530
I don't know if we can work together 
if you're so cheery and I'm not...

00:23:31.530 --> 00:23:33.330
It's because we're different
that we can have this friendly rivalry!

00:23:33.330 --> 00:23:35.250
We'd just wear each other out
and end up as sand.

00:23:35.250 --> 00:23:37.500
We'll scatter in the night skies like stars!

00:23:37.470 --> 00:23:39.960
<b><i>Sortie: </i></b>Noble And Fleeting<i><b></b></i>

00:23:37.500 --> 00:23:38.850
Next episode: "Sortie"

00:23:38.850 --> 00:23:39.960
"Noble and Fleeting"
